(We omitted step S (no action). Also we could skip some detach steps if not needed, but we kept them to free task profile.)
(We could possibly reduce steps by not detaching after preparing origin/destination, but we needed to switch. However we could have kept origin task profile linked while preparing destination by using a different route task profile? Not available. So we need to detach.)
(We could also avoid detaching after preparing origin and destination by using the same task profile for both preparations if we prepare one, then keep linked, prepare the other? Not possible because attach requires profile available. So we need to detach.)
(Thus the plan above seems minimal? Could we combine some steps? For example, after preparing origin, we could keep task profile linked, allocate vehicle to destination, then we cannot attach to destination because profile not available. So we must detach origin before attaching to destination. So detach needed.)
(After preparing destination, we could keep task profile linked to destination, then load/unload origin? No, origin load/unload requires origin task profile linked. So we need to detach destination before attaching to origin for origin load/unload. So we need detach after preparing destination.)
(Thus we need at least two detaches (after each prepare) to free profile for the other side's prepare. Then we need to attach for origin load/unload, then detach after origin load/unload to free for destination load/unload, then attach for destination load/unload, detach after, then attach for origin for assembly/auth. That's many attach/detach.)
(Could we reduce by doing origin load/unload before preparing destination? Let's think.)
(Alternative: Prepare origin (attach, prepare, detach). Then allocate vehicle to destination, attach task profile to destination, prepare destination, then we have task profile linked to destination. Now we need to do origin load/unload: need origin task profile linked, so detach destination, attach origin, load/unload origin, detach origin, attach destination, load/unload destination, detach destination, attach origin for auth. That's similar count.)
(Could we avoid detaching after load/unload by keeping task profile linked and then using it for auth? For origin, after load/unload we could keep task profile linked, then later we need it for auth anyway, so we could keep it linked through origin load/unload and not detach until after auth. Similarly for destination, we could keep task profile linked through its load/unload, then detach after destination load/unload to free for origin auth. Let's see.)
(We need origin task profile linked for auth (step R). So if we keep origin task profile linked after its load/unload, we can use it for auth without reattaching. Good.)
(Thus we can reduce detach/attach steps.)
(Let's design optimized flow:)
(1. Prepare origin: attach, prepare, detach (keep prepared, profile free).)
(2. Prepare destination: allocate vehicle, attach, prepare, detach (profile free).)
(Now both prepared, profile free.)
(3. Origin load/unload: attach origin, load origin, unload origin, (keep origin task profile linked) -> after unload, origin task profile still linked.)
(Now we have origin task profile linked, destination task profile not linked (since we detached after prepare). Good.)
(4. Destination load/unload: we need destination task profile linked. So we detach origin (free profile), attach destination, load destination, unload destination, (keep destination task profile linked) -> after unload, destination task profile linked, origin task profile not linked.)
(Now we have destination task profile linked, origin not linked.)
(5. For assembly and auth, we need origin task profile linked (for auth) and also need origin_availability_locked etc (we have). So we need to attach origin task profile again: detach destination (free), attach origin, then assemble leg, authorize loading, and we can keep origin task profile linked for goal.)
(Thus steps:)
(- Prepare origin (attach, prepare, detach))
(- Prepare destination (allocate vehicle, attach, prepare, detach))
(- Origin load/unload: attach origin, load origin, unload origin (keep linked))
(- Detach origin (to free profile))
(- Destination load/unload: attach destination, load destination, unload destination (keep linked))
(- Detach destination (to free profile))
(- Attach origin (for assembly/auth))
(- Assemble leg)
(- Authorize loading)
(- Release compliance certificate)
(- Dispatch shift)
(We also need to ensure we have vehicle allocated to destination before its load/unload (we already allocated in prepare destination step). Good.)
